# Lemon WMS — core context

Single Next.js app (not a monorepo): **office** `/dashboard` (Owner, OM, OW) and **floor** `/warehouse` (WM, WW). Shared DB and APIs; dashboard leans on shadcn/ui, floor uses custom touch-first UI.

## Stack (short)

- Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind 4, pnpm
- Prisma 7 + PostgreSQL (`lib/prisma.ts` singleton, client under `src/generated/prisma`)
- Auth: custom JWT — `POST /api/auth/login`, `POST /api/auth/floor/login`, logout, refresh; `src/middleware.ts` enforces role → `/dashboard` vs `/warehouse` (403 across sides)
- Data fetching: Axios (`lib/axios.ts`); no React Query in this repo
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod; auth state: Zustand

## API layout

- Office: `src/app/api/dashboard/*` (warehouses, zones, bins, users, devices, items, home, stock, …)
- Floor: `src/app/api/warehouse/*`
- Shared: `src/app/api/auth/*`, `errors`, `logs` (stub), `seed/users` (dev)

## Business logic

Put domain logic in **`src/lib/entities/<domain>/`** (focused modules). Route handlers stay thin and call entities; do not add a separate `lib/services/` layer.

